/* Shape scale — retuned to the V2 design (DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §3.5).
 * Consume as: border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-medium);
 *
 * WHY THIS DEVIATES FROM THE STOCK M3 SCALE
 *  V2 uses 8 / 10 / 12 / 14 / 16 / 20 / 24 / pill. The stock M3 ladder
 *  (4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 28) has neither enough rungs nor the right ones, so the existing
 *  token NAMES are retuned in place and the two missing rungs are named in the
 *  M3-2025-expressive "*-increased" style rather than starting a parallel vocabulary.
 *
 *  token                 | M3 stock | V2  | V2 usage
 *  ----------------------|----------|-----|-------------------------------------------
 *  corner-none           |    0     |  0  | square surfaces
 *  corner-extra-small    |    4     |  8  | chips
 *  corner-small          |    8     | 10  | icon tiles (36dp navy squares)
 *  corner-medium         |   12     | 12  | small buttons, upload thumbnails
 *  corner-medium-increased |  --    | 14  | submit button            (added rung)
 *  corner-large          |   16     | 16  | list cards, alert bar, nav pill, stat cards
 *  corner-large-increased|   --     | 20  | feature cards, CTA, AR info card (added rung)
 *  corner-extra-large    |   28     | 24  | large content cards
 *  corner-full           |  1000    | 1000| CIRCLES ONLY (see the warning below)
 *
 * WARNING: corner-full IS A CIRCLE TOKEN, NOT A PILL TOKEN.
 *  Do not put it on anything whose width differs from its height.
 *
 *  CSS resolves an over-large border-radius by scaling ALL radii by one shared
 *  factor f <= 1, which preserves the stadium shape. UI Toolkit does NOT: it
 *  clamps each axis independently, rx = min(r, width/2) and ry = min(r, height/2).
 *  So on a 295x42 element a 1000px radius resolves to rx=147.5, ry=21 -- a full
 *  ELLIPSE (a lens), not a stadium. The token is only correct where width ==
 *  height, where both clamps land on the same number and you get the circle.
 *
 *  A STADIUM THEREFORE NEEDS r == height/2 EXACTLY. Larger re-opens the ellipse
 *  (rx keeps growing toward width/2); smaller is a plain rounded rect. Two ways
 *  to get it, and the rule for choosing:
 *
 *   - Height is authored in USS (every pill in this library but one). Write the
 *     literal half-height on the same rule as the height it halves:
 *         height: 40px;  border-radius: 20px;
 *     No runtime cost, still overridable by a screen stylesheet, and the pair is
 *     pinned by ShapeDisciplineTests so it cannot silently drift apart.
 *
 *   - Height is driven by content -- font metrics, wrapping, OS font scale --
 *     so it cannot be known at author time. Call MdShape.KeepStadium(element),
 *     which re-pins the radius to half the RESOLVED height on every
 *     GeometryChangedEvent. MvTag is the only current user: its height is
 *     padding plus TextCore's line box for the label face.
 *
 *  ShapeDisciplineTests fails the build if corner-full appears on a rule that is
 *  not a declared square, so a pill cannot quietly regress into a lens again.
 *
 * Components whose look shifts with this retune (intentional — the component restyle
 * slices re-point them where V2 disagrees):
 *  - 4 -> 8  : MdMenu, MdDropdown popup, MdSnackbar, MdTextField
 *  - 8 -> 10 : MdChip (V2 chips are 8 -> repoint to extra-small when MdChip is restyled),
 *              MdListItem state layer, Gallery swatches
 *  - 28 -> 24: MdDialog, MdBottomSheet top corners
 *  - unchanged: corner-medium (MdCard, MdFab small) and corner-large (MdFab,
 *              BeachesScreen cards). V2 wants 16 on cards, so MdCard moves from
 *              corner-medium to corner-large in its restyle.
 */
:root {
    --md-sys-shape-corner-none: 0;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-extra-small: 8px;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-small: 10px;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-medium: 12px;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-medium-increased: 14px;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-large: 16px;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-large-increased: 20px;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-extra-large: 24px;
    --md-sys-shape-corner-full: 1000px;
}
